  "content_description": "Balance Action Item",
  "content_text_body": "The goal is to discover what your employees believe contributes to a healthy work-life balance.\n\n### Send out a meeting invitation \n\nHere's a [sample email](Glint_Balance_Team_Email_Template) to help get you started.\n\nPrior to the discussion\n\nAnswer these questions for yourself so you know what to expect from the team:\n\n> * Think about a time when you were doing well in this area. What made it possible?\n\n> * What limits your ability to do well here?\n\n> * Can you think of other leaders in the company who are really good in this area?\n\n> * If you were coaching you, what advice would you give yourself to improve in this area?\n\nKeep in mind these [Discussion Pointers](Glint_General_Discussion_Tips).\n\n### Team discussion on Work-Life Balance \n\nBegin by going over the [Meeting Ground Rules](Glint_General_Team_Meeting_Ground_Rules).\n\nFollow this [Meeting Plan](Glint_Balance_Team_Meeting_Plan) to guide your discussion.  \n\n### Reflect \n\nWhat did you learn about yourself or each other from your discussion? Have you noticed any changes in your or the team's behavior? Are you all getting better at work-life balance? How might you continue to do better?",
